<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">7 January in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">7 events that happened on 7 January, from 1558 to 2015.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/france" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/france.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1558">1558 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">468 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">France captures Calais, England's last mainland possession</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">French troops under the Duke of Guise forced the surrender of Calais, held by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> since 1347. Mary I reportedly said that when she died 'Calais' would be found lying in her heart.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1610">1610 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">416 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Galileo first observes the moons of Jupiter</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Through his improved telescope, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/galileo-galilei">Galileo</a> saw small 'stars' beside Jupiter that he soon realised were orbiting it. Bodies circling another planet undermined the belief that everything revolved around Earth.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1785">1785 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">241 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Blanchard and Jeffries fly a balloon across the English Channel</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Frenchman Jean-Pierre Blanchard and the American John Jeffries crossed from Dover to the Forest of Guînes in a hydrogen balloon. They jettisoned almost everything, including clothes, to stay aloft.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1927">1927 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">99 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">First commercial transatlantic telephone service opens</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A radio-telephone link connected <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a> for paying customers. A three-minute call cost 75 dollars, and transatlantic telephone cables did not arrive until 1956.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1953">1953 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">73 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Truman announces the United States has built a hydrogen bomb</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In his final State of the Union message, Harry Truman disclosed that the US had developed the hydrogen bomb, tested in November 1952. Its power dwarfed the atomic bombs used against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1979">1979 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">47 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Vietnamese forces capture Phnom Penh and topple the Khmer Rouge</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a>'s army took the Cambodian capital, ending <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pol-pot">Pol Pot</a>'s regime, under which some 1.5 to 2 million people had died. A decade of Vietnamese occupation and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guerrilla-warfare">guerrilla</a> war followed.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/2015">2015 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">11 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Gunmen kill twelve at the Paris offices of Charlie Hebdo</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Two Islamist gunmen attacked the satirical weekly Charlie Hebdo, killing twelve people including leading cartoonists. Millions marched in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> days later under the slogan 'Je suis Charlie'.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a></div></div></li></ol>
